{"title":"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as a four-place <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Decimal\" title=\"Decimal\">decimal</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417bb95d611844f9abf4944000d9b6f2e77e4696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.abcd,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> represent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Digit\" title=\"Digit\">digits</a>, any of which could be zero.  It is desired to approximate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by a fraction whose numerator is 1 or 2 and whose denominator is an integer. The closest such fraction to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a2143c4537715b41b0b5e2a9b1e8b096b167a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 27.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" />  What is the number of possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The nearest fractions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105c152e9b0808ebcb08f834803179885242f254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> with numerator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300f5e92fcf456cb4d70336d2d3d074a7baba4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 13, \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"32\" height=\"37\" />; and with numerator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d82b0fb6f2b3beebe0c4844b74cd723e9cd1b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 26, \\frac 28 = \\frac 13, \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> anyway. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105c152e9b0808ebcb08f834803179885242f254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> to be the best approximation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the decimal must be closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97065d2c245dcb3f67b073523d6ff87699e929a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 27 \\approx .28571$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" /> than to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a953cddba24361826f44891ab4cc1e83f89669a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 13 \\approx .33333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a53ff4ce0d096622bd3dd3c7a1bcaa7e4db3171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 14 = .25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can range between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32f802182334faa27485db719eea715c66508e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac 14 + \\frac{2}{7}}{2} \\approx .267857$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a193a4e2c29f601e8ee312a7016cd2c7b0cfb5a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac 13 + \\frac{2}{7}}{2} \\approx .309523$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"42\" />. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/9453a08b7cddb31de6ace58807f6ed9895222cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = .2678, .3096$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />, it becomes closer to the other fractions, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240fdc1e8ab1079dd28c0940ad21aea573187429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.2679 \\le r \\le .3095$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> and the number of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b585a7dc920933b3a94b38c8b1866faddff16d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3095 - 2679 + 1 = \\boxed{417}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME\" title=\"1997 AIME\">1997 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016222541\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 200/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4594/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.562      1 -total\n 59.71%    7.501      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.54%    4.841      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3003:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016222541 and revision id 289194. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}